; expect: exit 0
; Structs by value and struct results, both ways between keel and C,
; checked in structs.c. keel hands the struct memory to C helpers (h_* hash
; it, fill_* write it), so what is tested is exactly what the calling
; convention moved: registers for small structs and float aggregates,
; copies for big ones, the stack when registers run out, and results in
; registers or through x8.

